<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
	
	<web-app xmlns="https://jakarta.ee/xml/ns/jakartaee" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="WebApp_ID" xsi:schemaLocation="https://jakarta.ee/xml/ns/jakartaee https://jakarta.ee/xml/ns/jakartaee/web-app_5_0.xsd" version="5.0">
	<!-- 
	    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
	    TOMCAT 10.1+ FILE COUNT / PARAMETER COUNT FIX
	    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
	
	    ERROR:  FileCountLimitExceededException: attachment
	    CAUSE:  Tomcat 10.1 introduced a default limit of 50 total parts
	            (text fields + file inputs combined) for multipart requests.
	            The DeliveryRegisterServlet form has ~48 text fields + 12 file
	            inputs = ~60 parts, blowing past the limit before even the
	            first getParameter() call fires.
	
	    TWO FIXES ARE REQUIRED — both must be applied:
	
	    FIX 1 — @MultipartConfig in DeliveryRegisterServlet.java
	    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
	    Add  maxFileCount = 20  to the annotation.
	    This raises the file-part limit for that specific servlet.
	    (Already applied in the DeliveryRegisterServlet.java output file.)
	
	    FIX 2 — Tomcat Connector  (conf/server.xml  OR  conf/context.xml)
	    ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
	    The Connector has a separate  maxParameterCount  attribute (default
	    10000 in older Tomcat, but effectively capped by the multipart
	    FileCountLimit in 10.1).
	
	    Open  <TOMCAT_HOME>/conf/server.xml  and find the HTTP Connector:
	
	        <Connector port="8080" protocol="HTTP/1.1"
	                   connectionTimeout="20000"
	                   redirectPort="8443"
	                   maxParameterCount="200" />   ← ADD THIS LINE
	
	    200 is safe for this form (60 real params + headroom).
	    Do NOT set it to -1 (unlimited) — that disables a DoS protection.
	
	    Alternatively, if you cannot edit server.xml (shared hosting),
	    add this to  <TOMCAT_HOME>/conf/context.xml  inside <Context>:
	
	        <Context>
	            <JarScanner .../>
	        </Context>
	
	    and set the system property at Tomcat startup:
	        -Dorg.apache.tomcat.util.http.Parameters.MAX_COUNT=200
	
	    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
	     -->
